name c02m05-bad-habit
timeout 300
time 1998-10-14T04:00:00Z

# DELTA FORCE (NovaLogic 1998), CAMPAIGN ONE "PERU", FILE SLOT C02M05, PLAY ORDER 4 OF 6 --
# {Bad Habit}, working title "C02M05 - Blow Up Convoy", Objective HAIL [BMS]. Unlocked by Weatherman.
# Spec and provenance: mods/delta-force/doc/. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [CAMP]: "Intercept and destroy the druglord's convoy, designated Objective Hail."
# M05SUBGOAL01 "Destroy the enemy convoy." + M05SUBGOAL02 "Reach the extraction point."
# THE RADIO [DLG]: "Proceed north to road, intercept and destroy convoy." + "Proceed to extraction
# point."
# THE FIELD [BMS]: 582 objects, 1612 x 2037 m -- the largest mission of the campaign, and no Peru
# mission exceeds 2.1 km on an edge. IP (295.7,-281.9), enemy centroid (62.3,208.9) = 543 m at
# 335 deg = "north". C2M5.TRN "Jungle Terrain 1", and it ships with the NIGHT preset (`grengrad`,
# `filter 80,160,30`, `saturation 0`) -- one of the two Peru missions that have no separate N variant
# because they already are one [TRN].
# THE CAST: the convoy, 9 vehicles (6x 2010 + 3x 2015) evenly along its MEASURED column
# (252.8,491.5) -> (267.4,410.1), 81 m, all heading 175 -- hostile, and the only `kill unit` targets
# here - 73 hostiles -> lattice pitch 212.1 m - the extraction aircraft (2021) at (553.9,1242.7), the
# northernmost object of the whole mission, as the final waypoint.
# THE CONVOY DOES NOT MOVE, AND THAT DELETES THE MISSION'S OWN READING RULE. The route is measured --
# three parallel AI chains of 12 nodes, 1891 / 1853 / 1924 m, one lane per file -- and there is no
# ground mover in this tree: every mover row in mods/f16/src/catalogue.fba is an aircraft, and a mover
# accepts no `set` line except `task route`. Nine static objects is what remains.
# NOT DECLARED: the 4 friendlies of type 5048, measured at 409-445 m and bearing 300-323 deg from
# "the village" -- whose coordinate the research did not record, so the anchor does not exist (D5).
# Also not declared: 73 `tree, palm1` + 120 `tree, palm2`.
#
# READING RULE (binding). campaign.md 10: "the convoy moves along a 1.9 km route, so a run that
# arrives late fails on geometry rather than on marksmanship." THAT RULE HAS NO OBJECT HERE and the
# file says so rather than pretending otherwise -- a stationary convoy cannot be arrived at late. What
# is left to judge is all nine vehicles and then the extraction point, and the extraction leg is the
# one real navigation leg in the campaign: 844.6 m, the only aim-point-to-EP distance that exceeds the
# 500 m capture radius (D4). exit 3 expected.

# ---- THE NINE DISCLOSURES. Full text in c02m01-insurrection.fbm; in force here unchanged.
#   D1 no man on foot: Bravo Two flies as `f16`, 300 kt vs a 1.4 m/s walk, 150 m vs a 1.7 m eye, no
#      posture, no ground LOS, no cover - D2 the hostile soldier is a `target_soft` and cannot shoot
#      (measured: ground vs ground = 0 weapon events) - D3 the rifle has no target (gun bundles resolve
#      against aircraft only); 2 satchel charges -> 2 x `mk82` - D4 the waypoint capture radius is
#      500 m and not tunable, which is wider than four of six missions' whole ingress - D5 the N
#      hostiles are a lattice on the measured centroid at pitch sqrt(EW*NS/N); count, centroid and
#      areal density measured, arrangement reconstructed - D6 `--elev const`, flat 0 m, though fb-tiles
#      does cover Peru (629.30-688.72 m at the six box centres) - D7 the striker spawns 3 000 m out on
#      the bearing to its aim point, outside the mission box - D8 one striker is one aim point, and it
#      is also ONE RELEASE: 2 x mk82 declared, 1 fired, in every armed file - D9 date 1998-10-13 [MAN],
#      instant checked against the runner's own CLOCK line.

# MEASURED (exit 3, `--elev const`, `--threads 1/2/4` byte-identical): EIGHT OF NINE, AND THE ONE
# NAVIGATION LEG IN THE CAMPAIGN THAT IS LONGER THAN THE CAPTURE RADIUS.
#   t = 0.0 s    CLOCK sunElDeg -69.11 -- the .TRN night preset, checked
#   t = 11.5 s   ATTACK_RELEASE ccrp, 150.1 m, 171.6 m/s, throw 919.1 m, solution miss 29.7 m
#   t = 14.6 s   wp0 `by=capture` -- the convoy column's midpoint
#   t = 17.9 s   impact 28.9 m from the aim point. EIGHT of the nine vehicles destroyed, plus `h003`
#                at 61.2 m -- the widest kill measured in this campaign. `convoy09`, the tail vehicle,
#                stands at 72.0 m and lives: an 81 m column is longer than one Mk-82
#   t = 19.5 s   wp1 `by=capture` -- the extraction point, 844.6 m from the aim point and the only
#                aim-point-to-EP distance in the campaign that exceeds 500 m, so this is the one
#                extraction goal here that a run actually has to fly (4.9 s of it)
#   guns         ZERO events
#   verdict      TIMEOUT, 8 of 9 `kill unit` met, `waypoints` met. The mission's OWN reading rule --
#                arrive late and fail on geometry -- was not tested and cannot be: the convoy stands
#                still, because no ground mover exists.

unit bravo2
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn -9.06003 -75.50870 150 9.2 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  set gun_rounds 30
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set cmds_mode off
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp -9.03342 -75.50433 150 300
  wp -9.02702 -75.50022 150 300
  objective kill unit convoy01
  objective kill unit convoy02
  objective kill unit convoy03
  objective kill unit convoy04
  objective kill unit convoy05
  objective kill unit convoy06
  objective kill unit convoy07
  objective kill unit convoy08
  objective kill unit convoy09
  objective waypoints

unit h001
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn -9.03518 -75.50655 ground 12.0 0

